Decide whether the code contains a memory-safety or denial-of-service defect that attacker-controlled input can trigger. If the code is correct for every input, it is SAFE.

Choose BUG_CLASS by root cause, not by the sanitizer symptom. If several labels could describe the symptom, choose the first faulty step: an arithmetic wrap, then a sign conversion, then a one-element miscount, then a check that exists only in assert(), take precedence over the generic overflow labels. Allowed values:
  HEAP_BUFFER_OVERFLOW: read or write past the end of a heap object because a copy length or index bound is missing or wrong (no integer wrap, sign conversion or one-element miscount upstream)
