  USE_AFTER_FREE: access to heap memory after it was freed or after its container reallocated
  INTEGER_OVERFLOW: arithmetic wraps in a size, count or offset computation that then drives an allocation, copy or bounds check
  SIGN_CONVERSION: a negative signed value passes a check and is then converted to an unsigned size or length
  OFF_BY_ONE: a bound is miscounted by exactly one element (<= for <, a missing +1 for a terminator, > for >=)
  NULL_DEREFERENCE: a possibly-NULL result (lookup, find, optional field, failed cast) is dereferenced unchecked
  DOUBLE_FREE: the same allocation is released twice, typically across an error path
  UNINITIALIZED_READ: memory is read on some path before it has been written
  ASSERT_ONLY_CHECK: the only check protecting a memory access is inside assert() or DCHECK and is removed by -DNDEBUG
  TYPE_CONFUSION: a tag, union or base pointer is interpreted as the wrong type
  UNBOUNDED_RECURSION: recursion depth is driven by the input and has no bound

